incompatible debt and reject incompatible marginal extrema. General reconstruction implementation remains pending. G1, G2, G15. |\ndocs/plans/accounting-mission-requirements.md:68:| MC09 | Construct historical families through a specified method, with honest scope and search completeness. U2, U3, D. | Define candidate templates, model-scope records, instantiation and constraint lowering, feasible/infeasible/unknown results, truncation and coverage evidence. | Specified finite template/slot construction and coverage rules in Ch. 6/Core 0. Northstar bridges are solved and checked within the declared scope; completeness concerns that model only. A compiler for arbitrary supported template registries remains pending. G1, G3. |\ndocs/plans/accounting-mission-requirements.md:69:| MC10 | Distinguish uncertainty about facts, disclosure readings, admissible accounting treatment, estimates, behaviour and future shocks. U2, P, D. | Specify the categories, dependencies and admissibility checks; show why a factual unknown, permitted election and unsupported treatment cannot be substituted for one another. | Specified six uncertainty kinds with separate admission/provenance/dependency rules in Core 0 and Chs. 6–8. Examples distinguish factual composition, permitted inventory election and unsupported treatment. Factual/assumption admission is now tested for the authored debt case; all-category semantic validation remains pending. G6, G15. |\ndocs/plans/accounting-mission-requirements.md:70:| MC11 | Preserve the economic memory and scenario responses needed when histories are aggregated or refined. U2, D. | Define required state by contract/lot/cohort, permitted grouping transformations, supported horizon/scenarios, exact versus approximate status and invalidation when the query changes. | Specified grouping keys, additive transition/report proof, exact/approximate status and query invalidation in Ch. 6/Core 0. Debt, lot and cohort counterexamples are given; a general equivalence checker or empirical approximate-cohort error bound is not established. G1, G16. |\ndocs/plans/accounting-mission-requirements.md:71:| MC12 | Add probabilities only under an explicit justified joint measure, and retain unweighted alternatives when weights are unsupported. U2, P, D. | Specify optional weight/prior/likelihood records, dependence, overlaps, updates and mass preservation; provide a worked weighted and unweighted example with clear interpretation. | Specified finite joint weighting and one-use likelihood update in Ch. 6/Core 0; exact posterior 3/11 and 8/11, mixture and retained unresolved mass are checked. Continuous inference requires a target-specific method and validation. G2, G6, G15. |\ndocs/plans/accounting-mission-requirements.md:82:| MC18 | Preserve joint conditional future outcomes, honest bounds and distinct failure/completeness states. U2, P, D. | Define result payloads and queries that retain branch/path dependence, distinguish sampled ranges from certified bounds and distinguish default from unsupported/numerically failed output without silent dropping or renormalisation. | Specified result cells, branch statuses, strict bound attainment and unresolved mass in Chs. 6, 8, 10/Core 0. Exact linear, joint-output and funding/default reference checks pass; general simulation/result-query implementation remains pending. G2, G3, G6. |\ndocs/plans/accounting-mission-requirements.md:91:| MC22 | Represent insurers' contract groups, claims, service/finance components, assets and reinsurance. U1, U2. | Define cohort/group state and movements, declared measurement approaches and interfaces, reinsurance links and a complete structural/roll-forward example; expand actuarial/accounting support. | Partially repaired: Ch. 9 and `sectors.json` give a complete short-duration PAA gross/reinsurance roll-forward and chain-ladder point calculation. Selected AASB 17 paragraphs and Mack technical sections inspected. Separate treaty PAA eligibility and recognition timing are explicit in Version 1.2; journal counterexamples vary transferred risk and non-performance independently. General measurement, transition, variable fees and uncertainty/RA estimation remain open. G7, G8, G16. |\ndocs/plans/accounting-mission-requirements.md:98:| MC24 | Specify the core language and IR completely enough for compatible independent implementations. U3, D. | Provide complete grammar/lexical rules, AST/IR schemas, types, context rules, built-ins, errors, package interfaces and source-to-IR-to-result fixtures, including the demonstration package. | Core 0 grammar, closed structural IR, built-ins, arities, context/domain rules and complete debt dependency package supplied. Authored expected IR and selected expression-to-result checks pass. A frozen 17-export registry and bounded debt static validator now pass positive and schema-valid negative cases. General compilation, package loading, remaining semantic conformance and independent implementability assessment remain open. G2, G12, G15. |\ndocs/plans/accounting-mission-requirements.md:100:| MC26 | Specify supported numerical/solver operations and their limits. U3, P, D. | Define formula fragments, reformulations, exact/approximate monetary treatment, rounding, strict-domain bounds, infeasibility/conflict evidence, timeout and resource behaviour. | Specified rational-linear/finite-choice scope, amount reformulation, quantisation distinctions and typed unknowns in Ch. 6/Core 0. Z3 checks 4.975 attained and 7.035 unattained and concrete histories. Nonlinear solvers and a production rounding/optimization layer remain pending. G3, G10. |\ndocs/plans/accounting-mission-requirements.md:116:| MC32 | Deliver a detailed, readable LaTeX/PDF document that governs the intended implementation. U3, P. | Explain the whole problem, justify chosen methods, stage mathematical prerequisites, define supported behaviour and disclose open scope; connect derivations and sources to complete examples and interfaces. Preserve mathematical/source fidelity during revisions and inspect the rendered result. | Revised Version 1.2 candidate, 11 chapters plus two appendices, full cases and supporting normative files. Build, rendered inspection and baseline-preservation review are recorded in `review/author-review.md`. Human comprehension, domain review and independent implementability acceptance remain pending. G1, G2, G4, G5, G7, G10. |\ndocs/plans/accounting-mission-requirements.md:123:| MC34 | Stage implementation without losing the full mission or concealing unresolved decisions. U1, U2, U3, P, D. | Maintain requirement-to-section/case/gap traceability, explicit current-versus-later support, dependency order, workload assumptions and open decisions. Re-audit after material changes and test interactions, not just individual rows. | Original 34 requirement/acceptance pairs preserved; assessments updated and MC35 added from U4. The reviewed repair plan and G1–G18 result map preserve current/later/source-blocked obligations; implementation order remains in Ch. 11. Wider mission and acceptance stay active. G1–G18. |\ndocs/plans/accounting-mission-requirements.md:124:| MC35 | Complete feasible internal preparation before paid professional review and minimise avoidable reviewer effort. U4. | Allocate every residual gap to internal work or a specific professional judgment; supply checked facts, dated sources, a proposed answer, counterargument and consequences before referral. Any later engagement has explicit user authority and an agreed bounded scope/cost. Keep human acceptance separate from continued internal work. | Standing rule installed in mission/AGENTS. All G1–G18 allocated in `review/internal-before-expert.md`; debt semantic checks, three source dossiers, journal checks and manuscript corrections completed. The review brief is unsent; actual-company facts, source and implementation tasks remain internal. No paid-review readiness, spending authority or savings estimate is claimed. The eight-year corpus, provenance checks, 20 regression tests and annotation preparation format were completed internally without professional engagement. |\n    status={'required':len(required),'observed':len(observed),'missing':sorted(required.keys()-observed.keys()),\n            'uncatalogued':sorted(observed.keys()-required.keys()),\n            'duplicate_ids':sorted(k for k in required.keys()|observed.keys() if required[k]>1 or observed[k]>1),\n            'failed_observations':[x['obligation'] for x in p04.OBSERVATIONS if x.get('passed') is not True]}\n    finish_protection(ROOT,protected)\n    source_after={p:digest(ROOT/p) for p in source_before}\n    stable=all(h is not None and source_after[p]==h for p,h in source_before.items())\n    passed=all(r['passed'] for r in reports.values()) and protected['passed'] and stable and bool(required) and not any(status[k] for k in ('missing','uncatalogued','duplicate_ids','failed_observations'))\n    command=shlex.join(['python3','-B','scripts/check_accounting_p04.py']+(sys.argv[1:] if argv is None else argv))\n    payload={'schema_version':'accdsl.p04.conformance.v1','passed':bool(passed),'obligation_status':status,\n        'tests':reports,'observations':p04.OBSERVATIONS,'protection':protected,'code_stable_during_check':stable,\n        'input_source_test_hashes':dict(protected['before'],**source_before),\n        'manifest':{'git_commit':'unavailable: existing marker is not a usable repository','command':command,\n            'working_directory':str(ROOT),'executable':sys.executable,'environment':{'python':platform.python_version(),'z3':z3.get_version_string()},\n            'hardware':'CPU only; CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES=-1; no accelerator framework imported','random_seeds':'N/A: exact deterministic fixtures',\n            'data_version':'p04-reconstruction-cases-v1 plus preserved borrowing/Northstar fixtures','started_utc':utc,\n            'wall_seconds':round(time.monotonic()-started,6),'plan':PLAN,'plan_sha256':source_before[PLAN],\n            'execution_inventory':INVENTORY,'changed_source_code_test_files':SOURCES,'changed_files':SOURCES+OUTPUTS,\n            'outputs':OUTPUTS[:2],'result':OUTPUTS[1]},\n        'requirement_coverage':{'MC08':'shared symbols, choices, views and joint queries','MC09':'declared posting templates and bounded coverage',\n            'MC10':'six structural admission categories with provenance; external eligibility not independently certified',\n            'MC11':'unhedged additive bullet-debt grouping with retained memory','MC12':'explicit finite joint weights and retained mass',\n            'MC18':'strict bounds and unfinished cells','MC26':'exact rational linear and bounded integer numerical operations'},\n        'unsupported':catalog['unsupported'],\n        'acceptance':{'engineering':bool(passed),'accounting_validity':'not established','forecast_validity':'not established','human_acceptance':'pending','whole_gap_closure':False}}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
