{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_20","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '62,119p' scripts/check_accounting_p03.py && sed -n '67,74p' docs/plans/accounting-mission-requirements.md && sed -n '78,79p' docs/plans/accounting-mission-requirements.md && sed -n '90,91p' docs/plans/accounting-mission-requirements.md\"","aggregated_output":"def capture_protection(root, historical_path, execution_path, writable=PHASE_FILES,\n                       required_paths=()):\n    \"\"\"Keep historical differences separate; never replace the execution baseline.\"\"\"\n    errors = []\n    inventories = []\n    for name in (historical_path, execution_path):\n        try:\n            inventories.append(_inventory(root, name))\n        except (OSError, ValueError) as exc:\n            errors.append(f'{name}: {exc}')\n            inventories.append({})\n    historical, execution = inventories\n    protected = sorted((set(historical) | set(execution) | set(required_paths)) - set(writable))\n    absent = sorted(set(protected) - set(execution))\n    if absent:\n        errors.append('execution inventory omits protected paths: ' + ', '.join(absent))\n    before = {p: digest(root / p) for p in protected}\n    return {\n        'historical_inventory': historical_path,\n        'execution_inventory': execution_path,\n        'inventory_hashes': {p: digest(root / p) for p in (historical_path, execution_path)},\n        'excluded_phase_files': list(writable),\n        'errors': errors,\n        'execution_baseline': {p: execution.get(p) for p in protected},\n        'before': before,\n        'missing_before_check': [p for p, h in before.items() if h is None],\n        'changed_since_execution_entry': [p for p in protected if before[p] != execution.get(p)],\n        'historical_differences': [\n            {'path': p, 'phase_entry_sha256': historical[p], 'execution_entry_sha256': execution[p],\n             'attribution': 'Predates this execution, as recorded by the supervisor pre-edit inventory.'}\n            for p in sorted(set(historical) & set(execution) - set(writable))\n            if historical[p] != execution[p]],\n    }\n\n\ndef finish_protection(root, report):\n    report['after'] = {p: digest(root / p) for p in report['before']}\n    report['changed_during_check'] = [p for p in report['before'] if report['before'][p] != report['after'][p]]\n    report['changed_inventory_records'] = [p for p, h in report['inventory_hashes'].items()\n                                           if h is None or digest(root / p) != h]\n    report['passed'] = not any(report[k] for k in (\n        'errors', 'missing_before_check', 'changed_since_execution_entry',\n        'changed_during_check', 'changed_inventory_records'))\n    return report\n\n\ndef obligation_status(catalog, observations):\n    required_counts = Counter(c['id'] for c in catalog['obligations'])\n    observed_counts = Counter(c['id'] for c in observations)\n    required, observed = set(required_counts), set(observed_counts)\n    return {\n        'obligations_required': len(required), 'obligations_run': len(observed),\n        'missing': sorted(required - observed), 'uncatalogued': sorted(observed - required),\n        'duplicate_ids': sorted(k for k in required | observed\n                                if required_counts[k] > 1 or observed_counts[k] > 1),\n        'failed_observations': [c['id'] for c in observations if c.get('passed') is not True],\n    }\n\n| MC08 | Preserve jointly consistent discrete alternatives and continuous unknowns across accounts, notes and dates. U2, D. | Define history-family and choice/constraint semantics; provide cases preserving linked alternatives and rejecting incompatible combinations without independent account-by-account selection. | Specified shared symbols, choices and joint formulas in Chs. 2, 6–8. Exact reference checks retain fixed/floating histories, reject incompatible debt and reject incompatible marginal extrema. General reconstruction implementation remains pending. G1, G2, G15. |\n| MC09 | Construct historical families through a specified method, with honest scope and search completeness. U2, U3, D. | Define candidate templates, model-scope records, instantiation and constraint lowering, feasible/infeasible/unknown results, truncation and coverage evidence. | Specified finite template/slot construction and coverage rules in Ch. 6/Core 0. Northstar bridges are solved and checked within the declared scope; completeness concerns that model only. A compiler for arbitrary supported template registries remains pending. G1, G3. |\n| MC10 | Distinguish uncertainty about facts, disclosure readings, admissible accounting treatment, estimates, behaviour and future shocks. U2, P, D. | Specify the categories, dependencies and admissibility checks; show why a factual unknown, permitted election and unsupported treatment cannot be substituted for one another. | Specified six uncertainty kinds with separate admission/provenance/dependency rules in Core 0 and Chs. 6–8. Examples distinguish factual composition, permitted inventory election and unsupported treatment. Factual/assumption admission is now tested for the authored debt case; all-category semantic validation remains pending. G6, G15. |\n| MC11 | Preserve the economic memory and scenario responses needed when histories are aggregated or refined. U2, D. | Define required state by contract/lot/cohort, permitted grouping transformations, supported horizon/scenarios, exact versus approximate status and invalidation when the query changes. | Specified grouping keys, additive transition/report proof, exact/approximate status and query invalidation in Ch. 6/Core 0. Debt, lot and cohort counterexamples are given; a general equivalence checker or empirical approximate-cohort error bound is not established. G1, G16. |\n| MC12 | Add probabilities only under an explicit justified joint measure, and retain unweighted alternatives when weights are unsupported. U2, P, D. | Specify optional weight/prior/likelihood records, dependence, overlaps, updates and mass preservation; provide a worked weighted and unweighted example with clear interpretation. | Specified finite joint weighting and one-use likelihood update in Ch. 6/Core 0; exact posterior 3/11 and 8/11, mixture and retained unresolved mass are checked. Continuous inference requires a target-specific method and validation. G2, G6, G15. |\n\n## M3 — Economic events, journals and forecasts\n\n| MC14 | Give scenarios and decision information explicit meanings. U2, P, D. | Define supported exogenous stress, observational-conditioning and intervention modes, or explicitly scope unsupported modes; enforce information dates and distinguish real-world from pricing measures. | Specified exogenous stress, observational conditioning, intervention preconditions and information capabilities in Ch. 8/Core 0. Finite conditioning, an information-date example and debt stress typing/provenance are checked; causal intervention execution and arbitrary information-policy enforcement remain pending. G6, G14. |\n| MC15 | Specify ordinary corporate operations and accounting across periods. U1, U2, U3, D. | Provide a bounded coherent package for revenue/collections, purchases/payments, inventory/costs, assets/depreciation, payroll, financing and applicable closing/tax assumptions, with explicit exclusions. | Specified bounded corporate package in Chs. 2, 8 with exact annual/interim and forecast fixtures. Delivery, collection, purchase, payment, costs, plant, payroll, debt, simple tax and closing reconcile. Real tax/revenue/lease/FX packages remain separate work. G4, G5. |\n| MC21 | Represent banks' liabilities, assets, deposits, capital and regulatory/economic constraints. U1, U2. | Define core bank structural records now and operation-level later methods for funding, credit, liquidity and capital, including accounting/prudential reconciliation and an appropriate worked case. | Partially repaired: Ch. 9 specifies bank origination, transfer, interest, allowance, cash funding and default; exact fixture balances and capital reconciliation pass. Prudential weights are illustrative; full allowance lifecycle, IFRS 9/CECL and jurisdictional capital rules remain open. G7, G8. |\n| MC22 | Represent insurers' contract groups, claims, service/finance components, assets and reinsurance. U1, U2. | Define cohort/group state and movements, declared measurement approaches and interfaces, reinsurance links and a complete structural/roll-forward example; expand actuarial/accounting support. | Partially repaired: Ch. 9 and `sectors.json` give a complete short-duration PAA gross/reinsurance roll-forward and chain-ladder point calculation. Selected AASB 17 paragraphs and Mack technical sections inspected. Separate treaty PAA eligibility and recognition timing are explicit in Version 1.2; journal counterexamples vary transferred risk and non-performance independently. General measurement, transition, variable fees and uncertainty/RA estimation remain open. G7, G8, G16. |\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
