raint lowering, feasible/infeasible/unknown results, truncation and coverage evidence. | Specified finite template/slot construction and coverage rules in Ch. 6/Core 0. Northstar bridges are solved and checked within the declared scope; completeness concerns that model only. A compiler for arbitrary supported template registries remains pending. G1, G3. |\n69:| MC10 | Distinguish uncertainty about facts, disclosure readings, admissible accounting treatment, estimates, behaviour and future shocks. U2, P, D. | Specify the categories, dependencies and admissibility checks; show why a factual unknown, permitted election and unsupported treatment cannot be substituted for one another. | Specified six uncertainty kinds with separate admission/provenance/dependency rules in Core 0 and Chs. 6–8. Examples distinguish factual composition, permitted inventory election and unsupported treatment. Factual/assumption admission is now tested for the authored debt case; all-category semantic validation remains pending. G6, G15. |\n70:| MC11 | Preserve the economic memory and scenario responses needed when histories are aggregated or refined. U2, D. | Define required state by contract/lot/cohort, permitted grouping transformations, supported horizon/scenarios, exact versus approximate status and invalidation when the query changes. | Specified grouping keys, additive transition/report proof, exact/approximate status and query invalidation in Ch. 6/Core 0. Debt, lot and cohort counterexamples are given; a general equivalence checker or empirical approximate-cohort error bound is not established. G1, G16. |\n71:| MC12 | Add probabilities only under an explicit justified joint measure, and retain unweighted alternatives when weights are unsupported. U2, P, D. | Specify optional weight/prior/likelihood records, dependence, overlaps, updates and mass preservation; provide a worked weighted and unweighted example with clear interpretation. | Specified finite joint weighting and one-use likelihood update in Ch. 6/Core 0; exact posterior 3/11 and 8/11, mixture and retained unresolved mass are checked. Continuous inference requires a target-specific method and validation. G2, G6, G15. |\n82:| MC18 | Preserve joint conditional future outcomes, honest bounds and distinct failure/completeness states. U2, P, D. | Define result payloads and queries that retain branch/path dependence, distinguish sampled ranges from certified bounds and distinguish default from unsupported/numerically failed output without silent dropping or renormalisation. | Specified result cells, branch statuses, strict bound attainment and unresolved mass in Chs. 6, 8, 10/Core 0. Exact linear, joint-output and funding/default reference checks pass; general simulation/result-query implementation remains pending. G2, G3, G6. |\n100:| MC26 | Specify supported numerical/solver operations and their limits. U3, P, D. | Define formula fragments, reformulations, exact/approximate monetary treatment, rounding, strict-domain bounds, infeasibility/conflict evidence, timeout and resource behaviour. | Specified rational-linear/finite-choice scope, amount reformulation, quantisation distinctions and typed unknowns in Ch. 6/Core 0. Z3 checks 4.975 attained and 7.035 unattained and concrete histories. Nonlinear solvers and a production rounding/optimization layer remain pending. G3, G10. |\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
